{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 47, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Fair traveler thou seekest a journey to Japan's shore\nA land of honor and virtue thou shalt adore\nThy trip shall begin on day one at dawn's early light\nIn Tokyo's great city where neon lights do take flight\n\nThou shalt visit the Tokyo Tower's lofty height\nAnd from its summit gaze upon the city's delight\nNext thou shalt stroll through the Imperial Palace's gates\nWhere ancient traditions and history do create\n\nOn day two thou shalt venture to the Meiji Shrine\nA sacred place of reverence and mystic shrine\nThou shalt walk through the forested grounds and feel\nThe peaceful ambiance that doth gently reveal\n\nOn day three thou shalt visit the Tsukiji Fish Market's throng\nWhere fresh seafood doth abound and the senses are strong\nThou shalt sample sushi and sashimi's delicate art\nAnd behold the bustling stalls where merchants do their part\n\nOn day four thou shalt travel to Nikko's sacred hill\nWhere temples and shrines do stand in grandeur's will\nThou shalt behold the Toshogu Shrine's golden light\nAnd feel the awe that doth inspire in the night\n\nOn day five thou shalt visit the Hakone's scenic shore\nWhere hot springs and volcanic peaks do abound in store\nThou shalt ride the Hakone Ropeway's cable car so fine\nAnd gaze upon the majestic Fuji's snow-capped shrine\n\nOn day six thou shalt journey to Kyoto's ancient land\nWhere temples and gardens do stand in a bygone hand\nThou shalt visit the Fushimi Inari Shrine's thousands of gates\nAnd behold the vermilion torii that doth create a sacred state\n\nOn day seven thou shalt stroll through the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove's hush\nWhere gentle rustling of leaves doth softly rush\nThou shalt visit the Kinkaku-ji Temple's golden glow\nAnd behold the serene beauty that doth softly flow\n\nThus endeth thy journey to Japan's sacred shore\nMay thy travels be filled with wonder and awe evermore.", "log